  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` in `src/cli/truncate.ts` and committed it as `54e44d6`. The four new tests in `test/cli/truncate.test.ts` pass when run on their own with `node --test`. I did not run the full `npm test` suite.\n\n- **Short text:** text already within `max` comes back unchanged.\n- **Long text:** longer text keeps both ends around a `…`. The result is never longer than `max` characters. When the kept characters can't be split evenly, the extra one goes to the start, so `truncateMiddle('abcdefghij', 6)` gives `abc…ij`.\n- **Tiny `max`:** a `max` of 0 returns an empty string, and a `max` of 1 returns just `…`.\n- **Unicode:** length is counted in code points, so emoji and other surrogate-pair characters aren't split.\n\nThe file didn't exist before, so I created it. I put the test under `test/cli/`, next to the other CLI tests.",
